WEBVTT

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.200
Does this sound familiar?

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:08.120
You're all excited to start knitting a
sweater, and bam, you've hit a roadblock.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.167
Maybe the fit wasn't right,
the yarn didn't cooperate,

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.960
or you realized too late that you
were missing some key skills.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.280
Knitting a Sweater isn't just about
casting on, it's about

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.080
planning for success.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.680
And today, I'll show you how to do that.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.840
Hi, and welcome back to Knit It Now.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.367
In our last video,
we talked about why knitting a Sweater

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.840
on a Knitting Machine isn't instant magic.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.080
It takes planning, skills, and practice.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.560
Today, we're diving into the first
and most important step,

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.487
planning your sweater design and making
sure you have the skills

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.440
to bring it to life.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:49.200
Think of it like building a house.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.200
You wouldn't start building
without blueprints, right?

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.320
The same goes for sweaters.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.720
A little planning now
saves frustration later.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:02.160
That means choosing the right pattern,
evaluating your yarn,

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:06.160
and making sure your design works
for you and your knitting machine.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.720
First, decide on your sweater style.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:13.720
Ask yourself,
do you want a pullover or a cardigan?

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:17.760
Are you looking for a relaxed
fit or something more tailored?

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.160
What sleeve style and sleeve
length do you like?

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.480
Now be honest.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:25.000
What's your skill level?

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:30.007
If you're new to machine knitting,
I recommend starting with a simple

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:31.160
Drop Shoulder Sweater.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:36.647
It's beginner friendly and it lets you
focus on the basics without a whole

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:38.200
bunch of shaping or fuss and fuss.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.280
For a great beginner friendly sweater
project, check out our course

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.280
called Your Second sweater.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:48.720
Here's a quick preview of what's included.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:03.560
And Remember, with Knit It Now patterns,
you can use any yarn,

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.360
any machine, and your own gage.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.880
No need to match a pattern's gage.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.287
About yarn.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:15.560
Not all yarns work well
with every knitting machine.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:22.160
Make sure your yarn matches your machine's
gage range and always, always swatch.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:27.127
Swatching helps you see how the yarn
behaves and ensures accurate

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:28.280
pattern calculations.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:34.320
A sweater It is investment in your time,
so start with the right foundation.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:37.840
Now, let's take a look
at a pattern and break it down.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:39.960
Casting on.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.080
Do you know how to create
a stable cast on for sweaters?

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:48.480
What about hems or ribbing or
that dreaded stockinette curl?

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:50.760
Shaping.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:54.280
Are you comfortable with neat
and tidy increases and decreases?

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:56.800
Can you work short rows?

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:58.720
Finishing.

00:02:58.753 --> 00:03:03.120
Do you know to neatly join seams
and add neck lines or hems?

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:07.847
Now, if any of these sound
intimidating, don't worry.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:13.007
You can always practice on a smaller
project and check out the Knit It Now

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.240
tutorial library in our
Skill Builders series.

00:03:17.417 --> 00:03:21.240
Members also have access to our entire
Custom Patty Library,

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:26.040
giving you the flexibility to create
sweaters that fit you, your gage,

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.360
your machine, and your style.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:35.047
The key The key is to match your sweater
design with your current skills or ones

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.840
you're willing to learn and practice.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.560
Challenge yourself, but don't
set yourself up for frustration.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:46.680
Start small, build confidence,
and then tackle more advanced designs.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.400
What sweater design are
you thinking about making?

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:51.760
Let me know in the comments.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.240
Are you ready to plan
your perfect sweater?

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:00.000
I've put together a free planning
checklist to help you get started.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.120
Download it using that link below.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:08.360
And if you need extra help, Knit It Now
has step-by-step resources to guide you.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:15.167
In our next video, we'll bust some common
myths and mistakes that can

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.440
derail your project.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.480
We'll see you soon and happy knitting.

